			"en": {
				"name": "PPSh-45 .45 ACP submachine gun",
				"shortName": "PPSh45",
				"description": "The PPSh-45 (Pistolet-Pulemyot Shpagina - \"Shpagin's submachine gun\") is an American reproduction of a Soviet submachine gun originally designed by Georgy Shpagin as a cheap, reliable, and simplified alternative to the PPD-40. Unlike it's predecessor, this submachine gun fires the slower, heavier, and fatter .45 ACP - delivering a hefty punch."
			}
		},
